   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:bfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/JW-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/JW-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/JW-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/JW-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Joshua Allan Westgard",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Abfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "According to my testing, the only way to avoid the binding of a system-generated prefix is to ensure that the first use of a particular namespace is via a PATCH request in SPARQL update syntax.  Any POST or PUT request with turtle, rdf-xml, or n3 payload will result in the binding of previously unused namespaces to system-generated prefixes.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Some documentation and a proposed workaround have been posted here: ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/Best+Practices+-+RDF+Namespaces"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/Best+Practices+-+RDF+Namespaces",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "In addition, I attach a copy of a shell script that can be used to \"pre-bind\" a desired set of namespaces.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
