     "body": "<p>According to my testing, the only way to avoid the binding of a system-generated prefix is to ensure that the first use of a particular namespace is via a PATCH request in SPARQL update syntax.  Any POST or PUT request with turtle, rdf-xml, or n3 payload will result in the binding of previously unused namespaces to system-generated prefixes.</p>\n\n<p>Some documentation and a proposed workaround have been posted here: <a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/Best+Practices+-+RDF+Namespaces\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/Best+Practices+-+RDF+Namespaces</a></p>\n\n<p>In addition, I attach a copy of a shell script that can be used to \"pre-bind\" a desired set of namespaces.</p>",
